   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about family",
     "texto": [
      "Family words usually take an article: en far (a father), en mor (a mother), et barn (a child). In Bokmål, en can also be used with many feminine words: en søster.",
      "In Norwegian, the possessive can come after a definite noun: broren min means «my brother»; literally, «the brother mine». The ending -en here means «the».",
      "Barn has the same form in the singular and plural: et barn, flere barn. For people, han («he») and hun («she») are used."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
